<repaired_code>
def find_roots(
    graph: "Graph", prop: "URIRef", roots: Optional[Set["Node"]] = None
) -> Set["Node"]:
    # Initialize roots set if not provided
    if roots is None:
        roots = set()
        # Add all subjects that appear as subjects of the property
        for s, o in graph.subject_objects(prop):
            roots.add(s)
    
    # Find non-roots (nodes that appear as objects)
    non_roots = set()
    for s, o in graph.subject_objects(prop):
        non_roots.add(o)
    
    # Remove non-roots from roots to get actual roots
    return roots - non_roots
</repaired_code>

The fixed code:
1. Handles the case when roots parameter is None by initializing an empty set
2. Collects all subjects that have the given property relationship
3. Identifies non-root nodes (those that appear as objects in the property relationships)
4. Returns the difference between roots and non-roots to get true root nodes
5. Uses the available Graph API methods (subject_objects) and Set operations as indicated in the Oracle Context

This implementation will properly find root nodes in the graph that have no incoming edges for the specified property.

